logix (1.2.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: the server install did not work on a fresh Ubuntu host. Nothing
    installed the Python dependencies; installing them into the system
    interpreter would have failed anyway under PEP 668; python3-venv was
    assumed present; and sudo was invoked even when already root. The
    dependencies now go into server/.venv.
  * Fixed: ops/serve.py and ops/go_live.py did not find that venv on Linux,
    where a venv's bin/python is a symlink to the system interpreter, and
    so died with ModuleNotFoundError: fastapi.
  * Fixed: exporting from the local dashboard failed with Permission denied
    on macOS and Linux, because reports were written to a root-owned
    system directory. An explicitly configured reports directory is still
    honoured exactly as given.

 -- Logix <noreply@github.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

logix (1.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Local workstation dashboard: Overview (current session, live CPU/memory/
    GPU/storage), Logs (searchable local history, paged for 10k+ sessions),
    Server (sync state with structured failure classes). Served on
    loopback by report_server.py; no new dependency.
  * Optional job_type/job_id session metadata, carried through the local
    logbook, the dashboard, the XLSX/CSV export, and server sync.
  * YASB status contract v1: state-driven bar_status.json instead of a
    rewritten-every-second timer string; legacy keys kept for compatibility.
  * Sync failure classification (network/auth/rejected/server/unknown) so
    the UI never has to parse an error string to decide what to show.
  * Fixed: a UTF-8 BOM in device.json or config.env could make an enrolled
    device look unenrolled (every sync returning 401 with a valid key on
    disk). Fixed: automatic session closes were dated at discovery instead
    of at the boot/cap boundary, which could turn an overnight lock into a
    25-hour session.

 -- Logix <noreply@github.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

